# BUGS

An encrypted volume's plain superblocks show its label, UUID, size and layout, when it was made, and how many commits and inodes it has had.
XTS shows which blocks changed between two copies of the disk.
A whole older copy of the disk, written back, mounts: nothing records which commit is the newest but the disk itself.
A volume can't be encrypted in place, nor its key changed.
Queries and live queries see the live volume only, though a snapshot keeps its indices.
There are no permissions or owners over Node, and no symbolic links.
Wildcards in a query scan; there are no trigram indices.
